    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **21 run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new Cp12 (3 tests: whitespace/case, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection) and the existing Cp01/Cp10/Cp11 that now depend on normalized addresses.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `TelephoneE164` helper).\n\n**New file** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java`: a package-private helper whose `normalize(raw)` trims, collapses internal whitespace runs to a single space, upper-cases, and expands street-type abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). It is idempotent and returns `\"\"` when nothing remains.\n\n**Changed the create (`POST /api/owners`) pipeline:**\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 normalizes the address, adds `\"address\"` to the required-field errors (\u2192 400) when it is blank *after* normalization, and republishes the normalized value into the request variable so it is stored and returned as `address`.\n- `EnsureUniqueHousehold` \u2014 address comparison for duplicate detection now uses `AddressNormalizer.normalize`.\n- `AssignHousehold` \u2014 the shared `householdId` derivation and member-matching now use `AddressNormalizer.normalize` for the address.\n\nThe `PUT` update pipeline (which uses `ValidateOwner`/`ApplyOwner` and no household functions) was untouched, matching the spec's \"whenever an owner is created\" scope. Class javadocs were updated to describe the new behavior. `lastName` comparisons keep their existing case-insensitive/whitespace-collapse normalization, since the spec only calls for address to change.",
